`--across-face SYSTEM/SERVICE` (#980 C1b; core §8.5, observer §7.5): a raw
observer across a constrained face subscribes by the scopes the contracts in
hand give for the address. That is each concrete resource's exact key and
each template's key with every parameter a wildcard, never `<ns>/zk2/**`,
under which every put would carry its key's text across the face. No
presence is read, since no descriptor crosses: keys resolve through
`--contracts` alone. `tests/live_zk2.rs`'s
`constrained_s7_a_tools_scope_across_a_face` runs the scope against a bus.

The cases here are its refusals, each made before a session opens, and each
this tool refusing what it was given: exit 2.

No descriptor crosses a face, so the scope comes from `--contracts`, and
without them there is none.

```console
$ zenctl echo --across-face host-a/tc
? 2
Error: --across-face builds its scope from the contracts in hand, since no descriptor crosses a face (observer §7.5): give --contracts

```

An address names one service. A wildcard there would subscribe wider than
what the tool reads.

```console
$ zenctl echo --across-face '*/tc' --contracts ../examples/zk2/tcgui/tc.netif.v1.toml
? 2
Error: --across-face */tc: system "*" is not a plain chunk ([a-z0-9]([a-z0-9._-]*[a-z0-9])?). Name one service, SYSTEM/SERVICE, each a plain chunk: a wildcard would subscribe wider than what this tool reads (core §8.5)

```

A selector typed beside it is narrowed to the face's scope, and one that
reaches none of it is refused.

```console
$ zenctl rate 'zk2/host-b/**' --across-face host-a/tc --contracts ../examples/zk2/tcgui/tc.netif.v1.toml
? 2
Error: zk2/host-b/** reaches none of the resources the contracts in hand give for host-a/tc across the face: type a selector under one of them, or none

```

A rule that reads presence or the doctor reads `@zk`, which does not cross a
face, so the watchdog refuses it there.

```console
$ zenctl watchdog --rule 'instance-gone host-a/tc' --across-face host-a/tc --contracts ../examples/zk2/tcgui/tc.netif.v1.toml
? 2
Error: watchdog --across-face: `instance-gone host-a/tc` reads presence or the doctor, which do not cross a constrained face (core §8.5): drop the rule, or ask it on the face's own side

```

A rule whose selector reaches none of the face's resources would watch
nothing there.

```console
$ zenctl watchdog --rule 'rate-below zk2/host-b/** 1' --across-face host-a/tc --contracts ../examples/zk2/tcgui/tc.netif.v1.toml
? 2
Error: watchdog --across-face: `rate-below zk2/host-b/** 1` watches zk2/host-b/**, which reaches none of the selectors across the face (zk2/host-a/tc/tc.netif.v1/state/interfaces/*/* + zk2/host-a/tc/tc.netif.v1/state/namespaces + zk2/host-a/tc/tc.netif.v1/stream/bandwidth/*/* + zk2/host-a/tc/freshness.v2/stream/heartbeat/tc.netif.v1)

```

`--face-policy FILE --face NAME` (#988 L4; core §8.1, §8.5, observer
§7.5) names the face the tool reads across: its session runs the face's
`[transport]`, its default `--timeout` is the face's `reply_timeout_ms`,
and where the face says `arq = false` each scope with a horizon is declared
again after two horizons of silence. A `link.v1` policy states none of that.

```console
$ zenctl echo --across-face lab/radio-a --contracts ../examples/zk2/link/radio.v1.toml --face-policy ../examples/zk2/link/radio.face.toml --face radio
? 2
Error: --face-policy ../examples/zk2/link/radio.face.toml --face radio: a link.v1 policy states no reply timeout and no transport: a far side reads a link.v2 policy (link.v2 §2.20)

```

The face is one the policy names.

```console
$ zenctl echo --across-face lab/radio-a --contracts ../examples/zk2/link/radio.v1.toml --face-policy ../examples/zk2/link/media/rf.face.toml --face sbd
? 2
Error: --face-policy ../examples/zk2/link/media/rf.face.toml --face sbd: the policy has no face "sbd"; its faces are radio

```

With a face policy and its face (#990 V1, observer §7.5), the scope is
what the face's plan lets cross, each service the policy lists taken to
implement every contract in hand. A plan the profile refuses gives no
scope: here the rf face lists `modem.v3/frames/fast`, and no contract in
hand declares it.

```console
$ zenctl echo --across-face h-3fa9c2d41b7e/rf0 --contracts ../spec/profiles/health/health.v1.toml --face-policy ../examples/zk2/zenoh-modem/faces/zenohd-rf0.face.toml --face rf
? 2
Error: --face-policy ../examples/zk2/zenoh-modem/faces/zenohd-rf0.face.toml --face rf: the face's plan is refused (link.v2 §2.3), so there is no scope (observer §7.5): error frame_unknown [face rf] modem.v3/stream/frames/fast: an entry of the face's frames names no frame resource of a listed interface (link.v2 §2.7)

```

A selector given that meets nothing the plan lets cross is refused, never
dropped silently, and each one is named: on rf0 only `frames/fast`
crosses, and no state's push.

```console
$ zenctl timeline 'zk2/h-3fa9c2d41b7e/rf0/modem.v3/stream/air/**' 'zk2/h-3fa9c2d41b7e/rf0/modem.v3/state/oper' --for 1 --across-face h-3fa9c2d41b7e/rf0 --contracts ../examples/zk2/zenoh-modem/modem.v3.toml --face-policy ../examples/zk2/zenoh-modem/faces/zenohd-rf0.face.toml --face rf
? 2
Error: zk2/h-3fa9c2d41b7e/rf0/modem.v3/stream/air/** + zk2/h-3fa9c2d41b7e/rf0/modem.v3/state/oper each reach none of the resources the contracts in hand give for h-3fa9c2d41b7e/rf0 that face "rf"'s plan lets cross (observer §7.5): type a selector under one of them, or none

```

The two come together, and only beside `--across-face`.

```console
$ zenctl echo --face-policy ../examples/zk2/link/media/rf.face.toml --face radio
? 2
error: the following required arguments were not provided:
  --across-face <SYSTEM/SERVICE>

Usage: zenctl echo --across-face <SYSTEM/SERVICE> --face-policy <FILE> --face <NAME> --namespace <NS> [SELECTOR]

For more information, try '--help'.

```
